# Workflow gates

- Read [prd/README.md](prd/README.md) before product work.
- **No product features** until it names an **active phase** and the relevant `prd/` doc exists.
- **No invented requirements** — repo-local PRD skills + `prd/` only (not Superpowers `brainstorming`; do not call ChatPRD MCP unless the **user** asks).
- **No application code** until local `implement-from-prd` is run and the **user** approves the plan.
- **Scope:** implement only the active Linear issue / PRD section unless the **user** expands it.
- **Linear issues:** link `prd/…` + acceptance criteria; do not paste the full PRD.

# Before PR is ready for user review

Run **`sql-gym-pre-review`**: **reviewer** agent (no commits) and **fixer** agent (commits) must not be the same role as blind self-review—the implementer does not approve its own judgment pass. Use **sql-gym-pre-review-reviewer** in a **new** agent/chat or readonly Task, then **sql-gym-pre-review-fix**, and repeat until the reviewer reports no blocking items. Do **not** check PR boxes or ask for **user** review while blocking reviewer findings remain.

Checklist (all must pass before handoff):

- [ ] local `check-prd-alignment` vs linked `prd/` section (no unapproved blocking gaps)
- [ ] Superpowers `code-reviewer` vs approved plan + [engineering.mdc](engineering.mdc) (blocking feedback addressed)
- [ ] [google-eng-practices](docs/references/google-eng-practices.md) review (blocking items fixed; `Nit:` optional)
- [ ] cursor-team-kit `deslop` on changed code (or N/A — docs-only)
- [ ] Tests/lint green, or state **CI not configured yet** and run `./scripts/validate-env.sh` (or stack lint/test when they exist); note what ran in the PR
- [ ] PR: summary, risks, test plan, PRD deviations (if any)

Escalate to the **user** for product/architecture decisions or if stuck—do not mark boxes done to bypass a failed check.

# Agent environment

Stable ops for agents (local and Cloud). Current phase, stack, and dev commands: [prd/README.md](prd/README.md), [README.md](README.md), and `./scripts/validate-env.sh`.

- **Linear MCP** for backlog (`TIM-` issues, [sql-gym project](https://linear.app/times-api/project/sql-gym-ce6a8985c99e)). If lookup fails, ask the **user** to fix MCP auth in Cursor settings.
- **GitHub PRs (Cloud Agents):** create/update with Cursor `ManagePullRequest`; inspect, mark ready, and merge with `gh`. Do not use `gh pr create` on Cloud VMs—it fails with `Resource not accessible by integration`. See [docs/github-pr-operations-for-agents.md](docs/github-pr-operations-for-agents.md).
- **No committed secrets.** When the app exists, document vars in `.env.example`. On Cloud VMs, ask the **user** to add secrets in Cloud settings—do not assume a local `.env`.

